    feat(example): a task board whose only store is DuckBrain (EXAMPLE-APP-001)
    
    - http: answer the CORS preflight BEFORE auth and allow X-API-Key + PATCH,
      exposing X-Durability/X-Total-Count. Probe 2026-11-05: OPTIONS on a declared
      table answered 401 with no Access-Control-* header, so no cross-origin app
      could ever call the table API (the old mount also ran after auth).
    - replay: an insert and its delete inside ONE commit window are dropped as a
      pair (same table+key+contentHash) instead of turning the namespace change
      feed into CHANGELOG_CORRUPT for every subscriber (REPLAY-BIRTH-DEATH-001).
    - examples/taskboard: boards/columns/cards declared in schema.json, CRUD via
      /api/ns/:ns/tables, drag-and-drop move (PATCH by pk), server-side assignee
      filter, per-table grant denial (403 + audit reason table_grant), SSE change
      feed, one-command start.sh; transcript + screenshot in docs/.
    - tests: new CORS/preflight suite (fails on the pre-fix mount order) and a
      same-window birth+death replay case (fails on pre-fix replay.ts).
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
